# Copy to .env. Never commit .env.
#
# Workflow spec §8: the secret surface was "very nearly empty" until
# 2026-08-13, when the database ended it. In the deployed environment these
# come from Vercel; `vercel env pull` writes them here.

# The deployed database. Injected by the Vercel-Neon Marketplace integration.
# Use the POOLED endpoint -- serverless concurrency against a direct
# connection limit is the classic failure.
DATABASE_URL=

# Tests. A dedicated `test` BRANCH of the Neon project -- never production.
# Docker was the original plan; it is not installed, so the check gate now
# goes over the network. Task 8 measures what that costs and reports it.
#
# Ruling 5 (2026-08-13): use the UNPOOLED host here, unlike DATABASE_URL
# above. Schema-per-file test isolation (db/testdb.ts) sets TENDERFOOT_SCHEMA,
# which db/index.ts turns into a `-c search_path=...` Postgres startup
# parameter. Neon's pooled endpoint (PgBouncer) rejects that startup
# parameter outright -- error 08P01, "unsupported startup parameter in
# options: search_path" -- so a pooled DATABASE_URL_TEST cannot open a pool
# at all once TENDERFOOT_SCHEMA is set. This does not reopen the pooled
# requirement above: that one binds the deployed application, where
# serverless concurrency against a connection ceiling is the real failure
# mode. A test process is one client against a dedicated branch; the
# connection ceiling problem doesn't apply here.
DATABASE_URL_TEST=

# API port. Defaults to 3003
PORT=
